I did not add the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access, and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need `http-client`. Neither is granted, so the world imports only `inference-llm`. Sending the input's text to an external service would also leak untrusted feed content. If those features are needed, they should be added to the node's authority in the graph, not in the body.

